Feature: KeePass viewing and editing
  Scenario: Reject a wrong key and discard an unsaved password change
    Given a TUI workspace
    And a password protected vault with nested and empty groups
    When I open the TUI at 120 by 35
    And I press "Down F4"
    And I type "wrong-master"
    And I press "Enter"
    Then the screen contains "Master password"
    And the screen does not contain "Build server"
    And the screen does not contain "wrong-master"
    When I type "test-master"
    And I press "Enter F4 Shift+Tab"
    Then the screen contains "fixture-password"
    When I press "Ctrl+C"
    Then the clipboard contains "fixture-password"
    When I press "Backspace"
    And I type "X"
    And I press "Esc"
    Then the screen contains "Save changes?"
    When I press "Esc"
    Then the screen contains "Ctrl+C Copy password"
    And the screen does not contain "Save changes?"
    When I press "Esc n Ctrl+U"
    Then the clipboard contains "builder"
    When I press "Ctrl+R"
    Then the screen contains "fixture-password"
    When I press "Enter"
    Then the clipboard contains "fixture-password"
    When I press "Ctrl+R"
    Then the screen does not contain "fixture-password"

  Scenario: Remember a vault key and edit its password
    Given a TUI workspace
    And a password protected vault with nested and empty groups
    When I open the TUI at 120 by 35
    And I press "Down F3"
    Then the screen contains "Master password"
    When I type "test-master"
    And I press "Enter"
    Then the screen contains "Build server"
    And the screen contains "Empty group"
    And the screen contains "Servers"
    When I press "Enter"
    Then the clipboard contains "fixture-password"
    And the screen contains "copied"
    When I press "F4"
    Then the screen contains "View mode"
    When I press "Esc F4"
    Then the screen contains "Build server"
    And the screen contains "[Edit]"
    When I press "F4"
    Then the screen contains "Ctrl+C Copy password"
    When I press "Tab Tab Tab Tab"
    And I type "-rotated"
    And I press "F2 Esc F3 Ctrl+R"
    Then the screen contains "fixture-password-rotated"
    When I press "Enter"
    Then the clipboard contains "fixture-password-rotated"
    When I press "Ctrl+L F3"
    Then the screen contains "Master password"

  Scenario: Search the default tree, delete an entry, and undo the deletion
    Given a TUI workspace
    And a password protected vault with nested and empty groups
    When I open the TUI at 160 by 35
    And I press "Down F4"
    And I type "test-master"
    And I press "Ctrl+R"
    Then the screen contains "test-master"
    And the screen contains "◉"
    When I press "Ctrl+R Enter"
    Then the screen contains "Empty group"
    And the screen contains "Servers"
    When I type "servers"
    Then the screen contains "Build server"
    And the screen contains "Filter: servers_"
    When I press "F8"
    Then the screen contains "Delete this KeePass entry?"
    When I press "Enter"
    Then the screen does not contain "Build server"
    When I press "Ctrl+Z"
    Then the screen contains "Build server"
    And the screen contains "undone"
